course: dictionary
lesson: 773
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Bearing is one of them. Context tells you which meaning the writer means. «The travellers arrived, bearing gifts.» Here bearing means carrying, because travellers carry gifts.
explain: «Ball bearings let the wheel turn smoothly.» This bearing is a part of a machine, not a person carrying anything. Ask: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In maths and map reading, a bearing is a direction. Clues like north, degrees and three figures tell you this. «A bearing of 090 degrees is east.» When you lose your bearings, you do not know where you are, so the word is about direction in a different way.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Bearing can be a noun (a bearing) or a verb (bear, bears, bore, borne, bearing).
fact: «Ball bearings» are a part of a machine that lets a wheel turn smoothly.
fact: A bearing is a direction measured clockwise from north, always written with three figures: 090 is east.
fact: «Lose your bearings» means not knowing where you are.
exercise: «The travellers arrived, bearing gifts.» What does bearing mean here? | *Carrying | Sleeping | Shining | Losing
exercise: «Ball bearings let the wheel turn smoothly.» What is a bearing in this sentence? | A kind of road | A type of bird | A direction on a map | *A part of a machine that lets a wheel turn smoothly
exercise: A bearing of 090 degrees is which direction? | North | South | West | *East
test: Ella says she has lost her bearings in the woods. What does this mean? | She has found her bike | *She is not sure where she is | She is sure of her way | She is very hungry
test: «She was bearing the pain bravely.» What does bearing mean here? | Turning smoothly | Shining brightly | *Putting up with | Carrying gifts
exam: «The rain may have a bearing on when we finish the walk.» What does have a bearing on mean? | Point to the north | Carry a heavy load | *Have an effect on | Turn very smoothly
